{"text": "The graph above shows. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The numbers of very hot days. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Defined as days. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> With the highest daytime temperature reaching 35˚C or above. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In six cities. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 2023 and in 2024. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Among the six cities. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Cairo showed a greater number of very hot days. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Than any other city. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 2023 and in 2024, respectively. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Beijing was the only city. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Whose number of very hot days in 2024 was smaller. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Than that in 2023. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Among the cities shown in the graph. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 2024. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The number of very hot days in Manila. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Was greater than that in Rome. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Santiago had the smallest number of very hot days. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 2023 as well as in 2024. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Among the cities above. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In Washington, D, C. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The number of very hot days in 2024. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Was more than three times that in 2023.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "g", "r", "a", "p", "h", " ", "a", "b", "o", "v", "e", " ", "s", "h", "o", "w", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "n", "u", "m", "b", "e", "r", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "h", "o", "t", " ", "d", "a", "y", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "D", "e", "f", "i", "n", "e", "d", " ", "a", "s", " ", "d", "a", "y", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "W", "i", "t", "h", " ", "t", "h", "e"